EN = [
"Morris the Guide: 'Half a day north from the healer's hut. The prison has no sound. When there is no sound, you have arrived.' And below that. 'I drew the way back as well. Be sure to use it.'",
"Morris the Guide: Oh, and one more thing. That seed in the vegetable patch has sprouted. It's the size of a fingernail. It'll be a bit bigger by the time you're back.",
"Captain Roran: Head count. Survey Corps, one. …I count again when you're back.",
"Cells Locked From Inside",
"Every cell door is shut. The locks are fitted on the inside. The keys lie on the cell floors, in the ice. They locked themselves in and dropped the keys.",
"There is writing on the wall of the innermost and largest cell. Cut into the ice with the point of a knife. The handwriting is young.",
"\"I am Maledictus. I became king at sixteen and sat at the council at eighteen. They said that to divide the fire, one whole name must be fed to it. No one spoke. I spoke. I said, let us use the name of a prisoner.\"",
"\"I said it because I was afraid. That it would be my name. Because I was the youngest. But then that person stood up. The one who had been against it. And…\" Here the writing has been shaved away. He shaved it himself. And stopped partway.",
"\"I do not leave my eye in another's keeping. This prison is the prison of my prisoner. The prisoner is me. But I write this honestly. They said that if I became a guardian I would not die. Hearing that, I thought, a little, that it was a mercy.\"",
"Draugr Who Followed the King In",
"Chapter Four · The Sixth Eye",
"The Frost Prison",
"The king who locked the door with his own hand",
"Ice-Covered Cell · The Cook",
"You hold the torch to it and the ice cries. Water runs down the wall. Writing comes to light. Scratched with the handle of a ladle.",
"\"Olla, cook. His Majesty will not eat carrots. He eats them only if they are grated in. I am the only one who knows that, so I came.\"",
"A pot is frozen to the cell floor. The ladle still stands in it. She was stirring to the last.",
"Melt the ice",
"Ice-Covered Cell · The Drummer Child",
"The second cell has a low ceiling. The writing is at knee height. That was the height of the one who wrote it.",
"\"Fin, drummer. Twelve years old. When His Majesty became king at sixteen, I beat the drum. His Majesty was shaking, so I beat the time slowly. I came to beat it slowly for him here, too.\"",
"There is a drum. Its skin has frozen and split. One drumstick lies pointing toward the door. Toward the tomb chamber.",
"Archivist Isabel: (She presses the back of the hand holding her pen against her eyes.) …Twelve years old. Two years older than Mia.",
"Ice-Covered Cell · The Teacher",
"The wall of the third cell is full of writing. Corrections of spelling. She copied here what the king wrote on the wall of the tomb chamber, and corrected the mistakes. Though she could never show him.",
"\"Eda, writing teacher. His Majesty gets his spelling wrong. More so when he is hurried. The day he came back from the council he got three wrong in one line. I did not ask what had happened. I should have asked.\"",
"The very last line. \"I heard that the one who stood up at the council that day laid a hand on His Majesty's shoulder on the way out. And said, 'It is not your fault.' His Majesty cannot believe those words. I believe them.\"",
"Torch",
"Strays Before the Tomb Chamber",
"Before the Tomb Chamber Door",
"You pick up the crown. It is iron. Not gold. The Frost Kingdom was poor. A few strands of hair are frozen to the inner band. It was not taken off in a thousand years.",
"A folded parchment is tucked inside the band. The folds are worn through into holes. It has been opened and folded countless times. Though the place to send it was only one door away.",
"You stand the crown on the floor before the door. Cold vapor comes through the gap and circles the crown once. There is the sound of someone coming close on the other side and sitting down. Leaning their back against the door.",
"Archivist Isabel: (She puts her mouth to the gap in the door and reads the letter, clearly, word by word.)",
"Set down the crown",
"Archivist Isabel: The one who passed it off and the one who took it on spent a thousand years with a single door between them.",
"The Voice in the Gap of the Tomb Chamber Door",
"Cold vapor comes through the gap in the door. Within it someone speaks. It is not the voice of a king. It is the voice of a boy. \"You're not Brother. The footsteps are different.\"",
"\"I hear you put five to sleep. I heard the sound. Each time an eye closed, the ice here grew one layer thinner. I am afraid. I have been afraid for a thousand years. But now I am also tired of it.\"",
"\"The grey cloak told me. That if I opened the door he would give me a life without end. Like his own. I thought that was a good thing. Until I saw that man's face. In a thousand years that man has not smiled once.\"",
"\"Every time he came, that man asked the same thing. 'Do you remember that person's name?' I do not. No one does. That person, of their own will… no. That is not for me to say. That man must hear it for himself.\"",
"\"Let me ask one thing. You hold an ember, so once you will not die. When that once is used up, are you not afraid?\"",
"Isabel, Taking It Down",
"Archivist Isabel: (Quietly) Please answer him. I'll only write.",
"▷ …I'll answer.",
"\"I am afraid. That is why I fight beside someone who will write my name down.\"",
"\"I am not afraid. It is because there is an end that I walk.\"",
"Strays Guarding the Prison",
"The king who stopped at eighteen",
"Tell the grey cloak. The promise is withdrawn.\nAnd that person… did not blame you.",
"Captain Roran: One. The medicine bottle. The grey powder at the bottom of my medicine bottle. He came to my room the day before I set out with the twelve.",
"Captain Roran: Two. The coins. The six on the priests' pillows. The crests of six kingdoms. Whoever holds dies like those has been around for a thousand years.",
"▷ Three. The sheet in the lowest drawer. The two hundred and eleventh asking.",
"Captain Roran: He asked for a name, they say. Asked a machine. Two hundred and eleven times. That's not what a villain does. That's what someone who has lost something does. That's what confuses me.",
"Archivist Isabel: Four. Twenty-nine portraits. The same gloves. Five. The grey cloth on the eighth seat. Six. The words the king asked us to pass on. 'That person did not blame you.'",
"Archivist Isabel: Seven. My mother's last page. I haven't read it in fifteen years. It's the one thing I didn't hand over when the Elder said he would look at it first. I'm going to read it today. In front of the Elder.",
"▷ Are you afraid?",
"Archivist Isabel: Yes. But, you see. For twenty years I drank the tea he made me. When I ran a fever, he sat up through the night. I don't think all of that was a lie. Even a liar makes real tea. That's what frightens me more.",
"Archivist Isabel: Let's go. I've packed what I need for writing. Two pens. I think one of them is going to break.",
"Elder Erwin: You have come. Isabel too. Put down everything you have brought. No need to go through it piece by piece. It is all mine.",
"Elder Erwin: So there was a note. In the captain's wallet. And you hid it. …Well done. I would have hidden it too.",
"Archivist Isabel: Elder. Are all twenty-nine of them you?",
"Elder Erwin: Yes. I changed my name twenty-eight times. Only Erwin is real. It was my first name. That person gave it to me. At the last, I wanted to be here under that name.",
"Archivist Isabel: And my mother?",
"Elder Erwin: Elena read to the end. And then she came and asked me. As you do now. I told her the way to the far end of the Void. That the answer was there. Knowing she would not come back. …I make no excuse.",
"Elder Erwin: I cannot recall that person's name. For a thousand years. The face, the voice, the habits, I remember them all, and only the name is gone. The seven fed that person to the fire. I will gather the fire again and make it give up what it swallowed. One name.",
"▷ The King of Frost asked us to tell you. That person did not blame you.",
"Elder Erwin: (He says nothing for a long time.) …I heard. From the doorframe. That child was too timid ever to lie. And so I understand it even less. If there was no blame, why was I left behind?",
"Elder Erwin: I ask one last time. Give me your embers. With yours as well it will be over sooner. And no one hurt.",
"▷ My answer… you'll hear it now.",
"Guard the flame, guard the seals.\n…The third line I erased myself. Because it was a line I could not keep.",
"You pretend to hold out the ember, buying time for Isabel to fall back with the lantern.",
"\"Guard the flame, guard the seals.\" You refuse him with the oath he taught you.",
"Archivist Isabel: That thing on the back of his hand. I thought it was a pattern of flames. But there were strokes. It's a letter. One letter.",
"Archivist Isabel: The burned groove on the armrest of the eighth seat. The sixth groove. The width of a finger. …It was the Elder who touched it. A thousand years ago. That letter passed onto his hand.",
"Archivist Isabel: He holds one of the eight letters of the name in his own hand and cannot read it. On the back of his own hand.",
"▷ (You sit down beside her without a word.)",
"Archivist Isabel: …Thank you. The lantern can be lit again. There's half a jar of ink left. Not now. In a little while.",
"The one who swore to guard the flame took the flame. To find a single name.",
"So the lantern has gone out.\nYou who hold embers, do not come. …And yet you will come.",
"The Elder's Chest",
"The things inside the chest are laid out in order. Twenty-nine staffs. Twenty-nine seals. Spectacles, prayer beads, a worn hat. Things labeled as the relics of the Elders through the ages.",
"Every staff handle is worn in the same place. Where the right thumb rests. And every one is scorched in the same place. Where the back of the hand touches.",
"At the very bottom is a very small pen case. A boy's. Inside the lid, in a neat adult hand: \"Write slowly. Write names clearly. — Your Master\" Where the signature was, a hole has been burned through.",
"A Thousand Years of Diaries",
"One whole wall of shelves is diaries. The same format, the same handwriting. More than three hundred volumes. You pull out any one and look at the first line. \"Today again I cannot recall the name.\"",
"Another volume. \"Today again I cannot recall the name.\" Another. The same. The first line is the same every day. Only beneath it is the day's business written.",
"The volume from fifteen years ago: \"Elena read to the end. I sent her to the Void. Isabel cried, looking for her mother. I have decided to teach her to write. It is not atonement. I will come to need that child's hand. …It is not atonement.\" The last line is written twice.",
"The last page of the newest volume: \"The Survey Corps are good people. That person would have liked them. That person would have stopped me from doing this. That is why I must get the name back. Get it back, and be scolded.\"",
"The Plans of the Memory Gate",
"Plans are laid under the glass of the desk. A gate. The Gate the Survey Corps has opened countless times. The handwriting is the Elder's. The paper is a thousand years old.",
"Fine lines are drawn along the frame. Lines running from the thing that falls inside the Gate pass over the threshold and gather at a single point. Beside that point: \"Flows to: the brand.\"",
"\"Put to sleep outside a Gate, the share bursts and scatters (backlash). Put to sleep inside a Gate, the share pools. When six have pooled, the wick can be called.\"",
"A line added in the corner much later. The ink is fresh: \"A worry. A name the archivist writes in ink of ash cannot be eaten by the fire. Each time that child writes a guardian's name, one strand of the share stays bound to the name. That child does it without knowing what it does. Out of habit. Like her mother.\"",
"Chronicle of Vestalia · The Names Written So Far",
"Hargen · Isolde · Merwin\nHors · Helvar · Sirok · Skor\nCornelia and the three hundred and thirty-two · Nerakyss · Malkuth\nThe son who was given no name · The gatekeeper of the garden · Maledictus",
"Captain Roran: Let me set it out. Six shares have pooled in him. The seventh is Arden. Grand Master of the Flame Knights. That knight who came in your dreams.",
"Captain Roran: He will wake Arden. Then we have to put him to sleep. If we don't, the seal bursts. Put him to sleep outside a Gate and it's backlash. You saw the frozen sea.",
"Captain Roran: Put him to sleep inside a Gate and the seventh share goes to him. He knows that. He's laid it out so that he wins whatever we choose. It took him a thousand years.",
"▷ Then is there no way?",
"Captain Roran: There is one. The fire can't eat a name the archivist has written. If Arden's name is written down before he's put to sleep, the share doesn't go to him. It stays with the name. That's why he took that child. To keep her from writing it. Or to have her write a different name.",
"Ink Dot on the Basalt",
"A single dot is pressed on the black rock. Round. The same dot you saw in the corner of a book the first day you entered the archive. Touch it and it comes off on your finger.",
"A small arrow beside the dot. And words written one syllable at a time: \"Still. Walk. ing.\" Written while walking.",
"Captain Roran: …She makes her dots just like her mother. Elena drew her arrows crooked like that, too.",
"Ink Dots on the Fortress Wall",
"Three dots are pressed side by side on the rampart stone. Something that was not among Elena's marks. Beneath them: \"Three means 'don't stop.' I added one to my mother's marks.\"",
"Below that, smaller: \"The Elder holds my hand. It's hot. Even so, he doesn't let go. Like when he taught me to write. That is what frightens me most.\"",
"On the floor beside the dots are two lines of footprints. Not the prints of someone dragged. They walked side by side. The smaller one stopped now and then and put a hand to the wall.",
"Ignited Revenants Blocking the Way",
"Knights of the Rampart",
"Finale · The Nether",
"This time the daughter leaves the marks, and we follow",
"…Hot. This is ground I don't know. I'm going anyway. Find the dots.",
"Stop. A dot on the rock. Not dry yet.",
"Another on the rampart. Three in a row. I'll read that writing myself.",
"Twenty years ago I walked counting my people. Now I count dots.",
"The dots end before that gate. Go on ahead. We meet at the gate.",
"Fragment of Memory · Young Erwin",
"Master! Your hand, give me your hand!\n…The name. What was Master's name. I was calling it only a moment ago.",
"Ignited Berserkers Surrounding the Throne",
"Beacon Keepers Before the Throne",
"Chronicle of Vestalia · The Name Written on a Palm",
"Arden, Grand Master of the Flame Knights\nThe one who took the wick into his body. Not yet asleep.\n(There was no paper, so it was written on the archivist's left palm)",
"The Black Star in the Flames",
"Grand Master Arden, Falling Asleep",
"So you have come, you who hold embers. Though I told you not to.\n…It is good that you came. Now I will sleep a little.",
"Archivist Isabel: I'll read it. \"Erwin. I know you. The child of the scriptorium. The child that person sent out of the room and left in my care.\"",
"Archivist Isabel: \"That day I guarded the door of the council chamber. Inside, that person stood up. No one pushed. The seven could not even hold that person back. Out of fear. That is their sin. Not that they pushed, but that they did not hold back.\"",
"Archivist Isabel: \"That person told me: 'If the child tries to come in, stop him. That child will put his hand in.' I could not stop you. You slipped out between my legs. You were small.\"",
"Archivist Isabel: \"From within the fire that person saw you. Saw your hand. And smiled. There was no scolding. For a thousand years I could not pass that on to you. The fire stopped my mouth.\"",
"▷ The King of Frost said the same.",
"Archivist Isabel: Yes. 'There was no blame, I saw it.' Two people saw. The timid king, and the knight who guarded the door. …Maybe what the Elder needed was never the name. Maybe it was these words.",
"Elder Erwin: I am sorry to Elena. And to Roran. And to Kael. And to Cornelia. I never knew the words 'I am sorry' could be so light. Even after living a thousand years.",
"Elder Erwin: Isabel. Is your hand all right? …Yes. It will scar. Thank goodness it is not the hand you write with. No, 'thank goodness' is not for me to say.",
]
